        <ClinVarAccession Accession="SCV000839955" DateUpdated="2018-10-13" DateCreated="2018-10-13" Type="SCV" Version="1" SubmitterName="Human Genome Sequencing Center Clinical Lab, Baylor College of Medicine" OrgID="500199" OrganizationCategory="laboratory" OrgAbbreviation="HGSC-CL"/>
        <RecordStatus>current</RecordStatus>
        <Classification DateLastEvaluated="2017-10-13">
          <ReviewStatus>criteria provided, single submitter</ReviewStatus>
          <GermlineClassification>Pathogenic</GermlineClassification>
          <Comment>This c.1601G&gt;A (p.Arg534Gln) variant is known as the Factor V Leiden variant (legacy name p.Arg506Gln). Factor V Leiden variant is associated with thrombophilia due to activated protein C resistance [MIM:188055]. Studies suggest that the relative risk for venous thrombosis associated with the factor V Leiden variant in the absence of other acquired or environmental predispositions is approximately 4- to 7-fold for heterozygotes and 80-fold for homozygotes (PMID 16024978). This variant is classified as pathogenic. Homozygosity for this variant is also considered medically actionable.</Comment>
        </Classification>
        <Assertion>variation to disease</Assertion>
